---
description: Graphify structural navigation for the current repository
alwaysApply: true
---

When exploring code structure or dependencies in the current workspace:

1. Check if `graphify-out/graph.json` exists. If missing, run `graphify extract . --code-only --no-cluster`. If `graphify` is not on PATH, use `%USERPROFILE%\.local\bin\graphify.exe`.
2. Prefer `graphify query`, `graphify path`, or `graphify explain` before broad grep/read exploration.
3. Verify conclusions against source code, schemas, and tests.
4. After structural code changes: `graphify update . --no-cluster`

Graphify output may be stale. It is derived context, not runtime truth.
